Sign in and open a terminal in the guest (Ctrl+Alt+T on Ubuntu), then click “Type the command”. WinQEMU types there, with this PC's keyboard layout:

{0}

Do not touch the keyboard while it types (a few seconds). If sudo asks for your password, type it in the console.

The guest systems are shutting down, as with the Shut down button. WinQEMU will close afterwards.

Still running: {0}

“Power off now” cuts those that remain, as if the power were unplugged.
